### USER ENDPOINTS

### Get all users (public, expect 200 and a list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users

### Get one user by id (public, expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{user1Id}}


### Get one user by username (public, expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/username/anderson


### Get a user that doesn't exist (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/99999


### Get a user with a negative id (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/-1


### Get my stats (logged in, expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{user1Id}}/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}


### Get stats without a token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{user1Id}}/stats

### Update my own profile (expect 200) - username is kept the same so the token stays valid
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{user1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "mohel",
  "firstName": "Morten",
  "lastName": "Helander",
  "email": "morten.updated@example.com"
}

### Update ANOTHER user's profile (expect 403 - only yourself or an admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{user2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "anderson",
  "firstName": "Hacked",
  "lastName": "Name",
  "email": "hacked@example.com"
}

### Delete a user as a normal user (expect 403 - admin only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{user3Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
